#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nullspace for the Linux desktop (KDE Plasma on Wayland).

The trigger key works as the Essential key does on the phone. Squelch reads
the key and does the speech; this app does everything else:

  hold                  dictation (Squelch, unchanged)
  press                 capture the screen and the text on it; a card shows
                        it, and holding the key while it shows adds a note
  press, then hold      voice note
  double press          open Nullspace

squelch-ptt tells it about presses over the socket below ("capture", "open",
"note-start {json}", "note-end {json}"). Captures go to a hub, which files
them like the phone's: the one in Settings, or a hub on this computer (the
nullspace-hub user unit) when none is set. The window is the hub's page.
"""
